ready: 1
kind: sequence
id: recall.seq.index
display_id: SEQ-RECALL-INDEX
module: recall
title: Keep the search index current
summary: Applies every recorded memory change to the full-text and vector index in order, rebuilding when
  the embedding model changes.
trigger:
  trigger_kind: event
  text: A memory change is recorded, the daemon's index poll comes due, the daemon starts, or a purge
    asks for an immediate update
participants:
- sys.daemon
- id: db
  is:
  - sys.home
  label: Stack database
- id: model
  is:
  - sys.daemon
  label: Embedding model in the daemon
items:
- msg:
    from: sys.daemon
    to: db
    text: Read how far the index has followed memory changes
    constants:
    - recall.const.index-poll-seconds
    ops:
    - op: read
      entity: recall.data.index-state
- alt:
    branches:
    - when: there is no index yet, or the stack's embedding model differs from the one the index was built
        with
      items:
      - msg:
          from: sys.daemon
          to: db
          text: Rebuild the index from every active, dormant and forgotten memory
          ops:
          - op: delete
            entity: recall.data.search-index
          - op: read
            entity: memory.data.memory
            where: status IN (active, dormant, forgotten)
          - op: insert
            entity: recall.data.search-index
            set:
            - memory_id
            - version
            - kind
            - model_id
            - vector
          - op: update
            entity: recall.data.index-state
            set:
            - ledger_cursor = latest change id
            - model_id
            - rebuilt_at now
    - when: the index is current up to its cursor
      items:
      - msg:
          from: sys.daemon
          to: db
          text: Read memory changes after the cursor
          ops:
          - op: read
            entity: memory.data.memory-change
            by:
            - id greater than ledger_cursor
            order: id ASC
      - loop:
          while: changes remain
          items:
          - alt:
              branches:
              - when: the memory was purged or superseded
                items:
                - msg:
                    from: sys.daemon
                    to: db
                    text: Remove its full-text row and vector
                    ops:
                    - op: delete
                      entity: recall.data.search-index
                      by:
                      - memory_id
              - when: the memory was added or its content changed
                items:
                - msg:
                    from: sys.daemon
                    to: db
                    text: Update its full-text row from the current content
                    ops:
                    - op: upsert
                      entity: recall.data.search-index
                      by:
                      - memory_id
                      set:
                      - version
                      - kind
                - opt:
                    when: the stack has an embedding model
                    items:
                    - msg:
                        from: sys.daemon
                        to: model
                        text: Embed the memory's content
                    - msg:
                        from: sys.daemon
                        to: db
                        text: Store the vector with the model that made it
                        ops:
                        - op: update
                          entity: recall.data.search-index
                          by:
                          - memory_id
                          set:
                          - vector
                          - model_id
      - msg:
          from: sys.daemon
          to: db
          text: Advance the cursor to the last change applied
          ops:
          - op: update
            entity: recall.data.index-state
            set:
            - ledger_cursor
rationale: The index follows the change ledger instead of being called by every writer, so no write path
  can forget to update it. Purges run this sequence before they return, because the index holds memory
  text and must not keep deleted content after the caller is told it is gone. Brute-force similarity over
  one stack's vectors is fast enough for a personal store and keeps results deterministic. A missing model
  means word search only, never a stand-in vector that would mix incompatible results.
